<c.yellow>I demand an epic crash zoom.</c>

00:00:19.693 --> 00:00:20.690 line:85%
<i>(chuckles)</i>

00:00:20.690 --> 00:00:22.620 line:91%
<c.yellow>Let's finger-point.</c>
<c.colorCCCCCC><i>(both snap fingers)</i></c>

00:00:24.588 --> 00:00:28.223 line:91%
I'm with Beardyman,
who... makes... noises?

00:00:28.223 --> 00:00:30.001 line:85%
I don't know how to describe you.

00:00:30.001 --> 00:00:31.928 line:91%
Ten years ago,
I'd have called you a beatboxer,

00:00:31.928 --> 00:00:34.159 line:91%
but there's a lot more
equipment here these days.

00:00:34.159 --> 00:00:37.876 line:91%
<c.yellow>Ever since I started it, I've been
more interested in using technology</c>

00:00:37.876 --> 00:00:43.119 line:91%
<c.yellow>to morph my voice into...
whatever else I want it to be.</c>

00:00:43.477 --> 00:00:45.940 line:91%
And so, now you're gonna
do that to my voice.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:48.063 line:85%
<c.yellow>Oh yeah. Get ready.</c>

00:00:48.063 --> 00:00:49.687 line:85%
<c.yellow>You're gonna be a mega-star.</c>

00:00:53.076 --> 00:00:55.191 line:91%
<c.yellow>That's Tom Scott.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Hello!</c>

00:00:55.191 --> 00:00:57.745 line:91%
<c.yellow>I'm Beardyman.
What's going on?</c>

00:00:57.745 --> 00:01:00.414 line:91%
<c.green>Hello, Tom.</c>
<c.colorFFAAFF>Yo, yo.</c>

00:01:00.414 --> 00:01:02.614 line:91%
<c.yellow>What kind of music
do you like, Tom?</c>

00:01:02.614 --> 00:01:05.948 line:85%
My music tastes are really basic.

00:01:05.948 --> 00:01:07.693 line:85%
Like, regardless of the genre,

00:01:07.693 --> 00:01:09.855 line:91%
if you put "pop" in front of it,
I'm probably gonna be okay.

00:01:09.855 --> 00:01:11.980 line:85%
So, like, just basic as hell.

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:14.590 line:91%
<c.yellow>What about if you put "pop"
on the end of it, like "synthpop"?</c>

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:16.058 line:85%
Yeah. Yeah, that'll do.

00:01:16.058 --> 00:01:17.391 line:91%
<c.yellow>Or "post-pop"?</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Sure.</c>

00:01:17.391 --> 00:01:19.318 line:85%
<c.yellow>Okay. "Pop" on the beginning is...</c>

00:01:19.318 --> 00:01:21.565 line:91%
That is just pop made out of
the <i>Postman Pat</i> theme tune.

00:01:21.565 --> 00:01:22.604 line:85%
<c.yellow><i>(chuckles)</i></c>

00:01:22.604 --> 00:01:25.745 line:91%
My goal for this was, like, banger.
That's what I'm going for.

00:01:25.745 --> 00:01:26.585 line:85%
<c.yellow>Do you know about hyperpop?</c>

00:01:26.585 --> 00:01:31.056 line:91%
<c.yellow>Okay well, Charli XCX is part of
the whole PC Music collective.</c>

00:01:31.056 --> 00:01:34.455 line:91%
<c.yellow>She makes bangers,
and they're hyperpop-infused.</c>

00:01:34.455 --> 00:01:37.878 line:91%
<c.yellow>Caroline Polachek also makes—</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Yeah, let's aim for that.</c>

00:01:37.878 --> 00:01:39.899 position:56% line:85%
<c.yellow>Do you know about Caroline Polachek?</c>

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:43.388 line:91%
<i>(laughs) </i><c.colorEEEEEE>Let's aim for
two guys in a basement doing that.</c>

00:01:43.388 --> 00:01:44.885 line:91%
Yeah okay, fine.
<c.yellow>Yeah!</c>

00:01:44.885 --> 00:01:47.582 line:91%
<c.yellow>Okay, this is a good musical steer.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Alright.</c>

00:01:47.582 --> 00:01:49.867 line:85%
<c.yellow>Difficult to pull off! <i>(laughs)</i></c>

00:01:49.867 --> 00:01:51.571 line:91%
Well let's— let's—
<c.yellow>Let's do it.</c>

00:01:51.571 --> 00:01:54.668 line:91%
Let's go for somewhere around pop.
<c.yellow>No, 'cause— Look, 'cause like...</c>

00:01:54.668 --> 00:01:57.754 line:85%
<c.yellow>Your— Your singing voice...</c>

00:01:57.754 --> 00:01:59.703 line:85%
<c.yellow>is... no doubt sublime.</c>

00:01:59.703 --> 00:02:01.276 line:91%
<c.yellow>So let me see if
there's a bit of autotune.</c>

00:02:01.276 --> 00:02:03.277 line:91%
<c.cyan><i>(with faint vocoding)</i></c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>I'll just talk— Oh okay, right.</c>

00:02:03.277 --> 00:02:07.320 line:91%
So, I just need to give you a
<c.colorEEEEEE><00:02:04.640><c>♫ No-oo-</c><00:02:06.054><c>oo-</c><00:02:06.220><c>oo-</c><00:02:06.410><c>oo-</c></c>

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:10.548 line:91%
<c.cyan><i>(in chords)</i></c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>oo-<00:02:08.786><c>oo-</c><00:02:09.711><c>oo-</c></c>

00:02:10.548 --> 00:02:15.810 line:91%
<c.cyan><i>(with chorus and reverb)</i></c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>woow-<00:02:12.348><c>ohh-</c><00:02:14.101><c>ooo ♫</c></c>

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:18.529 line:85%
<c.colorCCCCCC><i>(with reverb, in unison)</i></c><c.colorEEEEEE> Nice.</c>

00:02:18.529 --> 00:02:21.198 line:91%
<c.yellow>There you are, man.
Yeah, okay.</c>

00:02:21.198 --> 00:02:23.664 line:91%
<c.cyan><i>(reverb off)</i></c><c.yellow> So yeah.
So we can totally do hyperpop.</c>

00:02:23.664 --> 00:02:28.611 line:91%
<c.yellow>'Cause it takes from K-pop,
which is dazzling and intense,</c>

00:02:28.611 --> 00:02:32.180 line:85%
<c.yellow>and it's just a lot, and...</c>

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:35.733 line:91%
<c.yellow>But there's a kind of squeaky-clean
commercialism to it.</c>

00:02:36.476 --> 00:02:38.475 line:91%
<c.yellow>Yes. This is great.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Yeah, let's do it. Okay.</c>

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:42.650 line:91%
<c.yellow>So right, I'm— instinctively,
I was just going to the mic.</c>

00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:44.541 line:85%
<c.yellow>But I'm not, right now.</c>

00:02:44.541 --> 00:02:46.746 line:91%
Hooh, okay. Alright.
This is on me. This is on me.

00:02:46.746 --> 00:02:48.954 line:91%
<c.yellow>So I'll tell you what we need.
Can you just put it really close?</c>

00:02:48.954 --> 00:02:52.626 position:64% line:91%
<c.yellow>Give me like a...
Just say the letter B as hard as you can.</c>

00:02:52.626 --> 00:02:55.073 line:85%
Like, buh.[/bə/]

00:02:55.073 --> 00:02:56.815 line:91%
<c.yellow>Mhm. But that's...</c>
<c.cyan><i>(hammers /bə/ sample)</i></c>

00:02:56.815 --> 00:02:58.477 line:85%
Okay, harder than that.

00:02:58.477 --> 00:03:00.649 line:91%
<c.yellow>Bit like, <i>(spits hard)</i></c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Yeah, okay.</c>

00:03:00.649 --> 00:03:02.650 line:91%
/bf/! No, that was bad.
<c.yellow>No, that was good.</c>

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:04.498 line:91%
<c.cyan><i>(hammers /bf/ sample)</i></c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>No, that's an F in that.</c>

00:03:04.498 --> 00:03:06.598 line:91%
Let me give that one more time.
<c.yellow>Take out the fricatives.</c>

00:03:06.598 --> 00:03:08.478 line:91%
/b/!
<c.cyan><i>(hammers /b/ sample)</i></c>

00:03:08.478 --> 00:03:10.219 line:85%
<c.yellow>That's a legit kick drum there.</c>

00:03:10.219 --> 00:03:12.205 position:56% line:91%
I tried to keep the aspiration back.
<c.cyan><i>(hammers /b/ sample as kick)</i></c>

00:03:12.205 --> 00:03:13.733 line:85%
<c.yellow>Okay, so...</c>

00:03:13.733 --> 00:03:17.172 line:85%
<c.yellow>Now I need something with a...</c>

00:03:18.078 --> 00:03:20.573 line:91%
<c.yellow>a plosive with a fricative,
please sir.</c>

00:03:21.073 --> 00:03:23.761 line:91%
<i>(gently)</i><c.colorEEEEEE> /pf/</c>
<c.cyan><i>(hammers /pf/ sample as snare)</i></c>

00:03:24.261 --> 00:03:25.740 line:85%
<c.yellow>That's great.</c>

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:27.740 line:91%
<c.yellow>Now, could you give me—
Could you, like...</c>

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:30.840 position:58% line:91%
<c.yellow>give me some sort of bongo-like sound
by just going like ogh.[/ɔʔ/]</c>

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:33.613 line:91%
<c.yellow>/ɔʔ/, something like that.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE><i>(gags faintly)</i></c>

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:36.048 line:91%
<c.yellow>No, you're being garroted.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Too far in the back of my throat.</c>

00:03:36.048 --> 00:03:39.197 position:63% line:91%
<c.yellow>Can you try, like, cluck like a chicken?</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Give me, like, linguistics terms.</c>

00:03:39.197 --> 00:03:42.143 position:59% line:91%
I did linguistics. I can give you a...
<c.yellow>I actually didn't do linguistics.</c>

00:03:42.143 --> 00:03:45.061 position:59% line:91%
<c.yellow>But I can say, "cluck like a chicken",
and that's...</c>

00:03:45.061 --> 00:03:48.704 position:64% line:91%
<c.yellow>In linguistics terms, what would you call
a <i>(clucks)</i>, like a "buck"?</c>

00:03:48.704 --> 00:03:51.822 line:91%
<c.yellow>Like a cockerel?</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>I honestly don't know.</c>

00:03:51.822 --> 00:03:54.590 position:69% line:91%
Alright, but I know what you're looking for.
<c.yellow>I thought you did linguistics, man(!)</c>

00:03:54.590 --> 00:03:56.993 line:91%
Back of the throat, explosion out.
<c.yellow>Yeah, sure.</c>

00:03:57.586 --> 00:03:59.387 line:91%
/pʷh/
<c.cyan><i>(hammers /pʷh/ sample)</i></c>

00:03:59.387 --> 00:04:04.298 line:85%
<c.cyan><i>(hammers samples as percussion)</i></c>

00:04:04.298 --> 00:04:06.259 position:63% line:91%
<c.yellow>That's good. I think I wanna layer that.
This is good for:</c>

00:04:06.259 --> 00:04:09.788 position:66% line:85%
<c.cyan><i>(performs percussion, hammers kick sample)</i></c>

00:04:09.788 --> 00:04:12.145 line:91%
<c.yellow>I'll pitch that down.</c>
<c.cyan><i>(kick samples at lower pitch)</i></c>

00:04:12.145 --> 00:04:15.924 line:85%
<c.cyan><i>(performs kick beat)</i></c>

00:04:15.924 --> 00:04:18.367 line:85%
<c.cyan><i>(melodic kick flourish)</i></c>

00:04:18.367 --> 00:04:20.841 line:85%
<c.cyan><i>(kick beat playback)</i></c>

00:04:20.841 --> 00:04:24.035 line:85%
<c.cyan><i>(adds high harmonic kick beat)</i></c>

00:04:27.842 --> 00:04:30.188 line:85%
<c.cyan><i>(adds low harmonic kick beat)</i></c>

00:04:34.654 --> 00:04:37.565 position:69% line:91%
That's magic. I've got no other word for it.
<c.cyan><i>(adds snare beat)</i></c>

00:04:37.565 --> 00:04:40.006 line:85%
<c.cyan><i>(modifies snare reverb)</i></c>

00:04:42.314 --> 00:04:44.450 line:85%
<c.cyan><i>(adds white noise to snare)</i></c>

00:04:46.927 --> 00:04:50.310 line:91%
<c.yellow>Alright. Now, can you give
a "tiss"? /ts/, /ts/.</c>

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:52.457 line:91%
<i>(sustained)</i><c.colorEEEEEE> /ts/</c>
<c.cyan><i>(/ts/ samples as open hi-hat)</i></c>

00:04:52.457 --> 00:04:56.182 position:59% line:91%
<c.yellow>Yep, and a few more.
Just variate the formant a little bit.</c>

00:04:56.182 --> 00:04:58.105 line:91%
Tsu.[/tsɸ/]
<c.yellow>Yeah.</c>

00:04:58.105 --> 00:04:59.870 line:85%
<i>(shorter)</i><c.colorEEEEEE> /ts/, /ts/</c>

00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:03.267 line:85%
<c.cyan><i>(performs dynamic hi-hat beat)</i></c>

00:05:03.267 --> 00:05:05.989 line:85%
<c.cyan><i>(hi-hats accelerate)</i></c>

00:05:11.037 --> 00:05:13.350 line:85%
<c.cyan><i>(adds reverb to hi-hat)</i></c>

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:15.811 line:85%
<c.cyan><i>(adds buzzy modifier to hi-hat)</i></c>

00:05:18.776 --> 00:05:19.973 line:85%
<c.cyan><i>(glitchy hi-hat fill)</i></c>

00:05:22.176 --> 00:05:23.734 line:91%
<c.cyan><i>(beat stops)</i></c>
<c.yellow>That's legit.</c>

00:05:23.734 --> 00:05:25.713 line:91%
<i>(laughs uproariously)</i>
<c.yellow>Wait, so how—</c>

00:05:25.713 --> 00:05:28.054 line:91%
That's incredible!
<c.yellow>Don't laugh, man. This is no joke.</c>

00:05:28.054 --> 00:05:29.806 line:91%
<c.yellow>You're gonna be a huge star.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>That's— That—</c>

00:05:29.806 --> 00:05:32.060 line:91%
<c.yellow>You're gonna be supporting
